    "introduction": [
      "The W3C Web of Things (WoT) describes a device or a service by a Thing Description: a JSON-LD document that names its properties, actions and events and states, in machine-readable form, which protocol operation reads, writes, observes or invokes each of them. A Thing Model is the reusable, instance-independent template a Thing Description is derived from.",
      "A Thing Description is therefore a complete, portable statement of what a Thing offers and how to reach it. What it is not is part of an address space: a Client that wants to browse, subscribe to or invoke a Thing has to read the document, understand its bindings and build the calls itself.",
      "This document defines an OPC UA registry for those documents and the address space they project into. Thing Descriptions and Thing Models are stored as canonical files, and the Server derives ObjectTypes, Objects, Variables, Methods and EventTypes from them, so that a Web of Things description becomes a browsable and subscribable part of the address space while the stored document remains the single source of truth."
    ],
    "draftBanner": "PROVISIONAL WORKING DRAFT — not normative, not endorsed by the OPC Foundation. The document number, the Mantis project identifier and every NodeId in this document are placeholders; the OPC Foundation assigns the real values."
  },

